      "writtenOn": "2023-11-29T07:54:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm, it\u0027s difficult as GKI versions can be differ by devices.\n\nProbably we can add GKI version as a new test variable, like:\n\n    @Parameterized.Parameters(name \u003d \"gkiVersion\u003d{0}\")\n    public static Collection\u003cObject[]\u003e params() {\n        return List.of(new Object[] {\"\"}, new Object[] {\"6.1\"}); /* to be amended whenever we add a GKI */\n    }\n\nDoes it look good? One caveat is that we may forget to amend the variable. Or any other suggestions?\n\n\u003e The tricky bit is too this in a way that doesn\u0027t impact our presubmit latency. I suggest running the suite on all supported kernels only in postsubmit\n\nIn the meantime I\u0027ll check this.",
      "parentUuid": "89f7edae_00ddf774",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 816,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 816,
        "endChar": 42
